import olympiad; import geometry; size(250);
defaultpen(linewidth(0.8));
draw((0,3)--origin--(10,0)--(10,5));
label("300 m",(0,3)--origin,W); label("1000 m",(0,0)--(10,0),S); label("500 m",(10,0)--(10,5),E);
draw((0,3)--(6,0)--(10,5),linetype("3 3")+linewidth(0.7));
label("$A$",(0,3),N); label("$B$",(10,5),N);
[/asy]

Equilateral triangle $ABC$ and square $BCDE$ are coplanar, as shown. $F$ is the intersection of $BC$ and $AD$. What is the number of degrees in the measure of angle $BAD$?

[asy]
size(70);
draw((0,0)--(20,0)--(20,20)--(0,20)--cycle);
draw((0,20)--(10,37.3)--(20,20));
draw((10,37.3)--(20,0));
draw((0,0)--(14.7,20));
label("$A$",(10,37.3),N);
label("$B$",(0,20),W);
label("$C$",(20,20),E);
label("$D$",(20,0),E);
label("$E$",(0,0),W);
label("$F$",(14,24),W);
